From 550024b49deb6ff726191645d718ab6d03b791f9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Seyoon Ragavan <complexzetaprime@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 18:41:24 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Constructible: spaceConstructible_poly moved from Savitch,
 statement unchanged; its dominance step through logSpace_eq
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The polynomial bounds' constructibility now sits beside the logarithmic and linear rows, so the
space hierarchy's corollaries can cite it without importing Savitch. Constructible imports
ClassNP.Transducer (the tail transducer); Savitch drops that import. The one proof change: the
bound logSpace n ≤ n + 1, which cited Machines/ARMWidth's logSpace_le_succ (outside Constructible's
closure), is proved through logSpace_eq.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../SpaceComplexity/Constructible.lean        | 167 +++++++++++++++++
 .../Complexity/SpaceComplexity/Savitch.lean   | 174 +-----------------
 2 files changed, 172 insertions(+), 169 deletions(-)

